      "description": "browserhive: checks the contents of behaviors/custom.jsonl against settings.behaviors. Every behavior the settings report as coming from the request must have its source here — that source arrived with the request and is recoverable from nowhere else once the response is discarded. The converse is not required: a line may have no matching entry, because a behavior can be placed in the page and then decline to act, and the code still ran.",
