      "description": "browserhive: a request or response record that says it had values replaced (BrowserHive-Redacted) has that field in its defined form and at least that many *** in the places it names. A record whose body was dropped for holding a hidden secret (WARC-Truncated: secret) holds no body and, if a response, is referred to by a metadata record with truncated: secret. Both describe the bytes they hold in their digests and HTTP Content-Length (BrowserHive WARC Profile 1.2.0). Passing does not mean the values are gone: wacz-validator does not know them, so a record that left a value in place, or replaced one without saying so, passes.",
