    },
    {
      "conformance": "MUST",
      "counts": {
        "error": 0,
        "info": 0,
        "warning": 0,
      },
      "description": "browserhive: in every response record (BrowserHive WARC Profile 1.6.0) and request record (1.7.0), the HTTP Content-Length, if there is one, states the number of bytes of the body the record holds, and the HTTP message has no Transfer-Encoding — also for a response that has no body to send, such as a redirect, a 304 or an answer to HEAD. A request record that holds a body has a Content-Length, and one with WARC-Truncated: unspecified (a body the producer could not obtain) holds none. Whether every request whose body was not obtained carries that mark cannot be told from the record.",
      "descriptionKey": "browserhive/http-message-length.desc",
      "docs": [
