    {
      "conformance": "MUST",
      "counts": {
        "error": 0,
        "info": 0,
        "warning": 0,
      },
      "description": "browserhive: browserhive:capture.random says whether the package holds the values the scripts of the captured page received at random — when recorded is true it carries documents, draws and truncated and no skipped, and the package holds random/values.jsonl and random/recorder.js, both declared in resources; when it is false it carries skipped (not-requested, withheld or failed) and the package holds neither entry, nor does a package whose document is withheld; each line is a JSON object with profile browserhive:random/1 and kind document or draw; document lines carry document (unique, ascending), url, frame (main or frame) and dpr, and record and date together, naming a response record in archive/ whose WARC-Date is date and whose WARC-Target-URI is url; draw lines carry document (of an earlier document line), seq (0, then one more per line of the document), api (Math.random, crypto.getRandomValues or crypto.randomUUID), caller, bytes for crypto.getRandomValues only, and value in the form its api sets; documents and draws are the numbers of those lines (WACZ Profile 1.26.0)",
      "descriptionKey": "browserhive/random-shape.desc",
