      "description": "browserhive: the page's text, its title and its accessibility tree are read from the rendered page, so a policy that kept the document's body out of the archive does not by itself keep them out. Checks browserhive:capture.document against the BrowserHive WACZ Profile (an archive that conforms to 1.10.0 is held to 1.10.0, where deny withholds nothing): withheld must be what the policies give for the document it names, in both directions; a withheld document leaves no text or title on its page entry (except an after-load snapshot's entry read from a document the policies do not withhold) and no accessibility tree; otherwise the tree names that document, not the requested URL",
